# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Modules in `utils/roles/applications/` MUST provide reusable helpers for reading, resolving, and validating application configuration. Helpers MUST stay independent of Ansible plugin entrypoints so the same code can be imported from filter plugins, lookup plugins, and library modules."
msgstr "Modules in `utils/roles/applications/` MOET herbruikbare helpers bieden voor het lezen, oplossen en valideren van de toepassingsconfiguratie. Helpers MOET onafhankelijk blijven van Ansible plugin entrypoints zodat dezelfde code geïmporteerd kan worden uit filterplugins, opzoekplugins en bibliotheekmodules."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Modules in `utils/roles/applications/services/` MUST NOT take over wider application-config concerns that belong to the sibling `config` module (path-driven `applications.<id>.<dotted>` reads, schema validation)."
msgstr "Modules in `utils/roles/applications/services/` MAG GEEN bredere toepassingsconfig-problemen overnemen die tot de broer of zus behoren `config` module (padgestuurd `applications.<id>.<dotted>` leest, schema validatie)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Modules in `utils/roles/applications/services/` MUST limit themselves to the service-graph derived from `meta/services.yml`: registry construction, dependency resolution between provider and consumer roles, and database backend selection per application."
msgstr "Modules in `utils/roles/applications/services/` Moest zich beperken tot de van de `meta/services.yml`: registry bouw, afhankelijkheid resolutie tussen provider en consument rollen, en database backend selectie per toepassing."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Modules in `utils/roles/validation/` MUST limit themselves to checking that role artefacts and their derived names obey the constraints documented in `docs/contributing/`: legal application identifiers, deployment-target invokability, container resource shape."
msgstr "Modules in `utils/roles/validation/` Moest zich beperken tot het controleren van die rol artefacten en hun afgeleide namen voldoen aan de beperkingen die in `docs/contributing/`: identificatie van juridische toepassingen, inzet-doelinvokbaarheid, containerhulpbronvorm."

