# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The classic failure shape (`DNS [OK]`, `TCP [OK]`, `TLS [FAIL] TimeoutError after 8s`) is an __MTU mismatch__, not a TLS-layer bug. Small packets (TCP-SYN, DNS replies) survive; the larger TLS-ServerHello with the certificate chain is dropped silently because the path MTU is below the bridge MTU and ICMP-needs-frag is filtered upstream. When `auth.docker.io` is OK but `ghcr.io` / `registry-1.docker.io` time out, the chain-length difference between hosts (Cloudflare-fronted ≈ small chain, GitHub/AWS ≈ large chain) confirms MTU as the cause rather than a blanket TLS block."
msgstr "De klassieke vorm van de storing (`DNS [OK]`, `TCP [OK]`, `TLS [FAIL] TimeoutError after 8s`) is een MTU mismatch__, geen TLS-laag insect. Kleine pakketjes (TCP-SYN, DNS antwoorden) overleef; de grotere TLS-ServerHallo met de certificaatketting wordt stil neergezet omdat het pad MTU onder de brug MTU ligt en ICMP-needs-frag stroomopwaarts wordt gefilterd. Wanneer `auth.docker.io` is OK maar `ghcr.io` ' `registry-1.docker.io` time out, het ketting-lengte verschil tussen hosts (Cloudflare-fronted ≈ small chain, GitHub/AWS ≈ grote keten) bevestigt MTU als de oorzaak in plaats van een deken TLS blok."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The classification of \"runnable\" and \"incompatible\" is computed by the Jinja filter `nextcloud_install_status` defined in [roles/web-app-nextcloud/filter_plugins/nextcloud_install.py](../../../filter_plugins/nextcloud_install.py). The filter inspects `rc`, `stdout`, and `stderr` from the OCC call and returns flags that drive `until`, `failed_when`, and `when`."
